Write $G_a^{u,x}=G^x_{[g(u)=a]}$. Expanding the commutator square gives  egin{align} & \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi}  igl(G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} - G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} igr)^\dagger  igl(G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} - G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} igr) \ot I \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & = 2 \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b} \Bigl( ra{\psi} G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} \ot I \ket{\psi} -  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} \ot I \ket{\psi}\Bigr), \end{align} using the projectivity of~$G$. To compare the two quartic terms, first note that  egin{equation} G^{u,x} = \sum_a G_a^{u,x} = \sum_a G^x_{[g(u)=a]} = G^x. \end{equation} The identity \eqref{eq:sum-of-gux} is exactly Proposition~ef{prop:post-processing-preserves} for the evaluation map $g \mapsto g(u)$. By ef{item:data-processed-consistency} and ef{prop:cons-sub-meas},  egin{align} G_a^{u,x} \ot I & \approx_{4\zeta} G^{u,x} \ot A_a^{u,x}
onumber \ & = G^x \ot A_a^{u,x}, \end{align} where the last equality is ef{eq:sum-of-gux}. Applying ef{prop:closeness-of-ip} once to the second term in ef{eq:gcom8} gives  egin{align} & \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} \ot I \ket{\psi}
onumber \ \approx_{2\sqrt{\zeta}} & \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} G^y \ot A_b^{v,y} \ket{\psi}. \end{align} The first boundedness-driven stability step is  egin{equation} \eqref{eq:apply-add-an-a-once} \approx_{\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} \ot A_b^{v,y} \ket{\psi}, \end{equation} which is ef{clm:g-comm-stability}. Applying ef{eq:add-an-a} once more and then ef{thm:commutativity-points}, we obtain  egin{align} \eqref{eq:gcom9} & \approx_{2\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} G^x \ot A_a^{u,x} A_b^{v,y} \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & \approx_{6\sqrt{\gamma(m+1)}} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} G^x \ot A_b^{v,y} A_a^{u,x} \ket{\psi}. \end{align} The second boundedness-driven stability step is  egin{equation} \eqref{eq:commuting-answer-swapped} \approx_{\sqrt{\zeta}+6\sqrt{\gamma(m+1)}} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} \ot A_a^{u,x} A_b^{v,y} \ket{\psi}, \end{equation} which is ef{clm:g-comm-stability2}. Using ef{eq:add-an-a} twice more and ef{prop:closeness-of-ip},  egin{align} \eqref{eq:gcom10} & \approx_{2\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} \ot A_b^{v,y} \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & \approx_{2\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} G_b^{v,y} \ot I \ket{\psi}. \end{align} Next, ef{item:data-processed-self-consistency} and the projectivity of~$G$ imply via ef{prop:two-notions-of-self-consistency} and ef{prop:two-notions-of-self-consistency-after-evaluation} that  egin{equation} G_a^{u,x} \ot I \approx_\zeta I \ot G_a^{u,x}. \end{equation} Applying ef{eq:new-fact-that-i-derived} twice with ef{prop:closeness-of-ip} turns ef{eq:gonna-cite-this-in-just-a-bit} into \[ \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G_b^{v,y} G_a^{u,x} G_b^{v,y} \ot I \ket{\psi}, \] which is the first quartic term from ef{eq:gcom8}. Collecting the ten approximation steps appearing between ef{eq:gcom8} and ef{eq:new-fact-that-i-derived} yields the bound \[ 48m igl(\gamma^{1/2}+\zeta^{1/2} igr), \] so the commutator norm is at most~$
u$.

If at least one of $\gamma$, $\zeta$, or $d/q$ is at least~$1$, then $
u \ge 30$ and the estimate is trivial from ef{prop:triangle-inequality-for-vectors-squared}. We therefore assume $\gamma,\zeta,d/q \le 1$. Expanding the commutator square gives  egin{align} & \E_{x,y} \sum_{g,h}  ra{\psi}  igl(G_g^x G_h^y - G_h^y G_g^x igr)^\dagger  igl(G_g^x G_h^y - G_h^y G_g^x igr) \ot I \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & = 2 \E_{x,y} \sum_{g,h}  ra{\psi} G_g^x G_h^y G_g^x \ot I \ket{\psi} - 2 \E_{x,y} \sum_{g,h}  ra{\psi} G_g^x G_h^y G_g^x G_h^y \ot I \ket{\psi}. \end{align} The first term is close to $ ra{\psi} G \ot G \ket{\psi}$, where $G=\E_x G^x$, by ef{prop:switch-sandwich} and ef{item:commuting-self-consistency}. For the second term, ef{prop:closeness-of-ip} and ef{lem:normalization-condition} yield  egin{equation} \E_{x,y} \sum_{g,h}  ra{\psi} G_g^x G_h^y G_g^x G_h^y \ot I \ket{\psi} \approx_{\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{x,y} \sum_{g,h}  ra{\psi} G_h^y G_g^x G_h^y \ot G_g^x \ket{\psi}. \end{equation} The first Schwartz--Zippel reduction evaluates the left factor at a random point:  egin{align} \eqref{eq:gcom4} & = \E_{x,y} \sum_{g,h}  ra{\psi} G_h^y G_g^x G_h^y \ot G_g^x \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & \approx_{ rac{dm}{q}} \E_{u,x,y} \sum_{a,h}  ra{\psi} G_h^y G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G_h^y \ot G^x_{[g(u)=a]} \ket{\psi}. \end{align} Indeed, the difference is  egin{equation} \E_{u,x,y} \sum_{g 
eq g',h}  one[g(u)=g'(u)]  ra{\psi} G_h^y G_g^x G_h^y \ot G_{g'}^x \ket{\psi}, \end{equation} and ef{lem:schwartz-zippel-individual} bounds this by $dm/q$. Next, apply ef{prop:closeness-of-ip} twice:  egin{align} \eqref{eq:evaluate-gcom-at-points} & = \E_{u,x,y} \sum_{a,h}  ra{\psi} G_h^y G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G_h^y \ot G^x_{[g(u)=a]} \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & \approx_{\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{u,x,y} \sum_{a,h}  ra{\psi} G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G_h^y G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G_h^y \ot I \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & \approx_{\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{u,x,y} \sum_{a,h}  ra{\psi} G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G_h^y G^x_{[g(u)=a]} \ot G_h^y \ket{\psi}. \end{align} A second Schwartz--Zippel reduction evaluates the right factor at an independent point:  egin{align} \eqref{eq:don't-understand-the-numbering-system} & = \E_{u,x,y} \sum_{a,h}  ra{\psi} G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G_h^y G^x_{[g(u)=a]} \ot G_h^y \ket{\psi}
onumber \ & \approx_{ rac{dm}{q}} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,b}  ra{\psi} G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G^y_{[h(v)=b]} G^x_{[g(u)=a]} \ot G^y_{[h(v)=b]} \ket{\psi}. \end{align} The difference is  egin{equation} \E_{u,v,x,y} \sum_{a,h 
eq h'}  one[h(v)=h'(v)]  ra{\psi} G^x_{[g(u)=a]} G_h^y G^x_{[g(u)=a]} \ot G_{h'}^y \ket{\psi}, \end{equation} and the same Schwartz--Zippel estimate again gives the loss $dm/q$. Now set \[ 
u_{\mathrm{evaluation}} = 48m igl(\gamma^{1/2}+\zeta^{1/2} igr), \] the error from ef{lem:comm-data-processed-g}. Apply ef{lem:comm-data-processed-g} to commute the evaluated families in ef{eq:evaluate-gcom-at-points-part-dos}; after one more use of ef{prop:closeness-of-ip} with ef{item:commuting-self-consistency}, the resulting quantity is $ ra{\psi} G \ot G \ket{\psi}$. Thus the second term in ef{eq:gcomterms} is also close to $ ra{\psi} G \ot G \ket{\psi}$. Combining the first-term estimate, ef{eq:gcom4}, the two Schwartz--Zippel losses, the two intermediate $\sqrt{\zeta}$ losses, and the evaluated commutation error $
u_{\mathrm{evaluation}}^{1/2}$ gives \[ 30m\left(\gamma^{1/4}+\zeta^{1/4}+(d/q)^{1/4}ight), \] where the constant $30m$ accounts for the $10m$ Schwartz--Zippel evaluation losses plus $20m$ from the $\approx$-chain in the first and second terms. This proves ef{thm:com-main}.

Let $H$ be the pasted submeasurement constructed in Definition~ef{def:pasted-measurement}. Lemma~ef{lem:h-b-consistency} implies  egin{equation} H_{[h(u,x)=a]} \ot I \simeq_{
u_6} I \ot B^u_{[f(x)=a]}. \end{equation} Applying ef{prop:triangle-sub} to ef{eq:h-b-consistency-at-a-point} and ef{eq:ld-abcon} gives \[ H_{[h(u,x)=a]} \ot I \simeq_{
u_6+\sqrt{8m\eps+4\delta}} I \ot A_a^{u,x}. \] Since $\sqrt{8m\eps+4\delta}\le 3m(\eps^{1/32}+\delta^{1/32})$ for $\eps,\delta\le 1$, the total error is at most \[ \sqrt{8m\eps+4\delta}+
u_6 \le 47k^2m\left(\eps^{1/32}+\delta^{1/32}+\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+(d/q)^{1/32}ight)\le 
u, \] which proves ef{item:ld-pasting-N-consistency-sub-measurement}. The completeness claim is exactly Corollary~ef{cor:ld-pasting-N-completeness}.

Its consistency is governed by the commutation of the slice measurements, but its completeness is subtler. The heuristic comparison is
\[
	\bra{\psi} H \ot I \ket{\psi} \approx \bra{\psi} G^{d+1} \ot I \ket{\psi}.
\]
Thus one would like to show
\begin{equation} \bra{\psi} G^{d+1} \ot I \ket{\psi}
	\approx \bra{\psi} G \ot I \ket{\psi}.
\end{equation}
The naive estimate would instead suggest
\begin{equation} \bra{\psi} G^{d+1} \ot I \ket{\psi} \approx 1-(d+1)\kappa,
\end{equation}
which is too weak for the induction.

The key input is that one can first show
\begin{equation} \bra{\psi} G^{d+2} \ot I \ket{\psi}
	\approx_\Delta \bra{\psi} G^{d+1} \ot I \ket{\psi},
\end{equation}
for a small error $\Delta = \poly(m)\cdot \poly(\eps,\delta,\gamma,\zeta,d/q)$. Writing the eigendecomposition $G=\sum_i \lambda_i \ket{v_i}\bra{v_i}$ and the induced spectral distribution $\mu(i)=\bra{\psi}(\ket{v_i}\bra{v_i}\ot I)\ket{\psi}$, this is equivalent to
\begin{equation} \Delta
	\ge \bra{\psi} G^{d+1} \ot I \ket{\psi} - \bra{\psi} G^{d+2} \ot I \ket{\psi}
	= \E_{i\sim\mu}[\lambda_i^{d+1}(1-\lambda_i)].
\end{equation}
The remaining comparison between $G$ and $G^{d+1}$ is then reduced to a scalar inequality.

Writing the eigendecomposition $G=\sum_i \lambda_i \ket{v_i}\bra{v_i}$ and the induced spectral distribution $\mu(i)=\bra{\psi}(\ket{v_i}\bra{v_i}\ot I)\ket{\psi}$, this is equivalent to
\begin{equation} \Delta
	\ge \bra{\psi} G^{d+1} \ot I \ket{\psi} - \bra{\psi} G^{d+2} \ot I \ket{\psi}
	= \E_{i\sim\mu}[\lambda_i^{d+1}(1-\lambda_i)].
\end{equation}

Let $M = \E_y \sum_o M_o^y$. The error to bound is  egin{align} & \E_{x,y} \sum_o \|(G^xM_o^y - M_o^yG^x)\ot I \ket{\psi}\|^2 
onumber \ ={} & \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} M_o^y (G^x)^2 M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} + \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} G^x (M_o^y)^2 G^x \ot I \ket{\psi} 
onumber \ & \qquad - \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} G^x M_o^y G^x M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} - \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} M_o^y G^x M_o^y G^x \ot I \ket{\psi}. \end{align} We compare all four terms with $ ra{\psi} G \ot M \ket{\psi}$. For the first term in ef{eq:g-commute-with-gg-error},  egin{align*} \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} M_o^y (G^x)^2 M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} & = \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} M_o^y G^x M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} \ & = \E_y \sum_o  ra{\psi} M_o^y G M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} \ & \approx_{2\sqrt{\omega}} \E_y \sum_o  ra{\psi} G \ot M_o^y \ket{\psi} 	ag{by ef{prop:switch-sandwich} and ef{eq:M-self-consistent}} \ & =  ra{\psi} G \ot M \ket{\psi}. \end{align*} For the second term,  egin{align*} \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} G^x (M_o^y)^2 G^x \ot I \ket{\psi} & = \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} G^x M_o^y G^x \ot I \ket{\psi} \ & = \E_x  ra{\psi} G^x M G^x \ot I \ket{\psi} \ & \approx_{2\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_x  ra{\psi} M \ot G^x \ket{\psi} 	ag{by ef{prop:switch-sandwich} and ef{lem:g-complete-self-consistency}} \ & =  ra{\psi} M \ot G \ket{\psi}. \end{align*} For the third term, first  egin{align} \E_{x,y} \sum_o  ra{\psi} G^x M_o^y G^x M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} & = \E_{x,y} \sum_{o,g}  ra{\psi} G^x M_o^y G_g^x G_g^x M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} 
onumber \ & \approx_{\sqrt{\chi}} \E_{x,y} \sum_{o,g}  ra{\psi} G^x M_o^y G_g^x M_o^y G_g^x \ot I \ket{\psi}. \end{align} This is the Cauchy--Schwarz estimate coming from ef{eq:M-commutes-with-G}. Next,  egin{equation} \eqref{eq:split-G-and-commute} \approx_{\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{x,y} \sum_{o,g}  ra{\psi} G^x M_o^y G_g^x M_o^y \ot G_g^x \ket{\psi}. \end{equation} Here the error is bounded using ef{item:ld-pasting-self-consistency}. Then  egin{equation} \eqref{eq:move-G-to-right-factor} \approx_{\sqrt{\zeta}} \E_{x,y} \sum_{o,g}  ra{\psi} G_g^x G^x M_o^y G_g^x M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi}, \end{equation} again by strong self-consistency of $G_g^x$. Since $G$ is projective,  egin{align} \eqref{eq:move-G-back-to-left-factor} & = \E_{x,y} \sum_{o,g}  ra{\psi} G_g^x M_o^y G_g^x M_o^y \ot I \ket{\psi} 
